# Delivery path

## Mermaid flowchart

<<mermaid>>
flowchart LR
    A[Author] --> B[DocLang AST]
    B --> C[Renderer]
    C --> D[HTML]
    C --> E[PDF]
    C --> F[DOCX]
    D --> G[Review]
    E --> G
    F --> G
<<end>>

# Service collaboration

## PlantUML sequence

<<plantuml>>
@startuml
actor Author
participant DocLang
participant Renderer
database Assets

Author -> DocLang: build validation fixture
DocLang -> Renderer: AST + resolved theme
Renderer -> Assets: render rich elements
Assets --> Renderer: themed images
Renderer --> Author: document output
@enduml
<<end>>

# Formula rendering

The quality gate compares the same formula in browser and offline paths.

<<math>>
E = mc^2
caption: "Mass-energy equivalence"
label: "eq:quality"
<<end>>

# Audience interaction

## Static poll

<<poll>>
question: "Which output should the reviewer inspect first?"
options: ["HTML", "PDF", "DOCX"]
multiple: false
<<end>>

## Static quiz

<<quiz>>
question: "Which renderer keeps interactive responses synchronized across viewers?"
options: ["The static document renderer", "A live websocket service", "The DOCX exporter"]
answer: 1
explanation: "A shared result requires a live channel. Documents show the answer and explanation statically."
<<end>>
